SO-101 robot model and meshes

soarm/robot/so101.xml and all 19 STL meshes in soarm/robot/assets/ are
copied without modification from MuJoCo Menagerie, robotstudio_so101,
commit ac6b2b09983786f3036cab1000221017fa2193b4:
https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie/tree/ac6b2b09983786f3036cab1000221017fa2193b4/robotstudio_so101

The upstream README credits The Robot Studio SO101 robot and includes
the attribution "developed by I2RT Robotics".

Menagerie derives the model from TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100. Its README
identifies aec17bbc256d1a7342d53aaa4950595d4c30b40d as the copied XML
version and links to the original MJCF at 608122e9ac330a753735f2e18aee73338e9ac407:
https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/blob/aec17bbc256d1a7342d53aaa4950595d4c30b40d/Simulation/SO101/so101_new_calib.xml
https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/blob/608122e9ac330a753735f2e18aee73338e9ac407/Simulation/SO101/so101_new_calib.xml

The Menagerie model and both cited TheRobotStudio revisions are licensed
under Apache-2.0. The original model license is retained at soarm/robot/LICENSE.
https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie/blob/ac6b2b09983786f3036cab1000221017fa2193b4/robotstudio_so101/LICENSE
https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/blob/aec17bbc256d1a7342d53aaa4950595d4c30b40d/LICENSE
https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/blob/608122e9ac330a753735f2e18aee73338e9ac407/LICENSE

tools/graspgenx/so101/gripper.urdf (in the repository, not in this package)
is derived from soarm/robot/so101.xml above: the gripper subtree rewritten
by hand as URDF for GraspGenX, the wrist camera mount and the primitive
collision geoms left out. It references the same meshes and carries the
same Apache-2.0 license; the file identifies itself as modified in its
header, as Apache-2.0 section 4 asks.
